<details><summary>Prerequisite: local versus global loops</summary>

A tile boundary is contractible: it can be shrunk to a point. A loop winding around the torus is noncontractible. Curvature controls the first kind. The two periods control generators of the second kind. See the [torus](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Torus), [discrete differential geometry](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discrete_differential_geometry), and [holonomy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holonomy) for broader context.

